  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Ryan Weathers handed them a shutout. They handed it back in the eleventh.",
    "what_this_means": "A perfect starter's line should not result in a loss. Weathers threw seven scoreless innings on three hits. The kind of performance that wins games. Instead, the Yankees spent the night chasing runners into dead ends, leaving sixteen men on base across eleven innings and converting only one into a run. Grisham's tenth-inning single broke through, gave them the lead they needed. Then nothing. The eleventh inning arrived, the defense folded, and a shutout became a loss. This is not a pitching failure. It is an offense that starved itself while the door stayed open. They had the game. They didn't finish it.",
